# Adversarial stress test for the deopt REENTRANCY-DEPTH guard
# specifically (as opposed to deopt_megamorphic_stress.zu, which is a
# flat loop and never nests deopts on the native stack at all).
#
# `rec` is genuinely self-recursive -- each call is still on-stack
# when its own recursive call happens -- and its return value
# alternates type by depth parity, the worst case for a speculative
# guard on `v = rec(n - 1)`'s result. If the guard mismatches at
# EVERY nesting level, a naive (unbounded) deopt-resume would recurse
# one native stack frame per recursion level, unboundedly, exactly
# the failure mode MAX_DEOPT_REENTRANCY exists to bound. Depth is
# picked well above both MAX_JIT_CALL_DEPTH (1024) and
# MAX_DEOPT_REENTRANCY (64) so this exercises the guard for real
# rather than staying under it by accident.

def rec(n) {
  if n <= 0 {
    return 0
  }
  var v = rec(n - 1)
  if is_number(v) {
    v = v + 1
  }
  if n % 2 == 0 {
    return n
  }
  return 's'
}

iter var i = 0; i < 50; i++ {
  echo rec(5000)
}
